  "_comment": "Curated community names for graph_refine.py. Keyed by a CONTENT SIGNATURE — the three highest-degree member ids, sorted and joined by '|' — not by community index, because re-clustering renumbers indices and an index-keyed name lands on whichever group happens to be numbered that way next time. Lives in scripts/ and not graphify-out/, because that directory is gitignored and a curated name written there is lost on a fresh clone. Anything not listed here still gets an accurate mechanical name ('{file} · {hub}'), which is honest but rarely useful: t() is the most-connected symbol in the app, so it wins 'hub' in several unrelated communities and they all came out called 'app.js · t'.",

